SEG = "LAW"
CAT = "fqLaw"
Q = [
    ("Under the Queensland Weapons Act 1990, weapon possession and use are subordinate to:",
     "Public and individual safety", ["A licensee's genuine reason", "The needs of shooting clubs", "The wishes of rural landowners"],
     "Section 3 of the Weapons Act 1990 says weapon possession and use are subordinate to the need to ensure public and individual safety. A genuine reason is needed for a licence, but it never outranks safety."),
    ("The stated object of the Weapons Act 1990 (Qld) is to:",
     "Prevent the misuse of weapons", ["Promote the shooting sports", "Register every rural property", "Fund firearm safety courses"],
     "Section 3(2) gives the object of the Act as preventing the misuse of weapons. Strict licensing, storage and carriage rules are the means to that end."),
    ("Which of these is a genuine reason for possessing a weapon under the Weapons Act 1990 (Qld)?",
     "Recreational shooting", ["Protecting your home", "Self-defence when travelling", "Deterring trespassers"],
     "Section 11 lists sports or target shooting, recreational shooting, an occupational requirement and the collection, preservation or study of weapons. Self-defence and home protection are not reasons, and s 57 says self-defence is not a reasonable excuse for carrying a weapon in public."),
    ("An applicant whose reason is recreational shooting can support it with:",
     "A landowner's written permission", ["A landowner's verbal permission", "A receipt for a new gun safe", "A hunting magazine subscription"],
     "Section 13(3) requires written permission from a landowner to shoot on the landowner's rural land, or proof of current membership of a prescribed body. Verbal permission does not meet the rule."),
    ("An applicant whose reason is sports or target shooting must provide proof of:",
     "Current club membership", ["Past competition results", "A rural landowner's permission", "Ownership of a target rifle"],
     "Section 13(2) of the Weapons Act requires proof that the applicant is a current member of an approved shooting club. Landowner permission supports recreational shooting, not target shooting."),
    ("An applicant whose reason is an occupational requirement must state:",
     "Why the job needs a weapon", ["How many shots they fire a year", "Which dealer they will buy from", "How long they have been shooting"],
     "Section 13(5) says the applicant must state why possession of a weapon is necessary in the conduct of their business or employment, such as a rural purpose on farming land."),
    ("A Queensland licence other than a minor's licence may be issued to an individual only if the person is at least:",
     "18 years old", ["16 years old", "17 years old", "21 years old"],
     "Section 10(2) of the Weapons Act allows a licence other than a minor's licence to be issued only to an adult, that is, a person aged 18 or over. Younger people may be eligible for a minor's licence."),
    ("The youngest age at which a Queensland minor's licence can be issued is:",
     "11 years", ["12 years", "14 years", "16 years"],
     "Section 10(2)(a)(ii) of the Weapons Act sets the minor's licence age at no younger than 11, within the age group set by regulation. A minor's licence ends when the holder turns 18."),
    ("A Queensland minor's licence stops being in force when the holder:",
     "Turns 18", ["Turns 16", "Finishes school", "Joins a club"],
     "Section 20(6)(c) of the Weapons Act says a minor's licence stops being in force when the licensee turns 18. The person then needs an adult licence to keep possessing weapons."),
    ("The longest term a Queensland licence for category A or B weapons can be issued for is:",
     "10 years", ["5 years", "3 years", "1 year"],
     "Section 20(1) of the Weapons Act limits a licence for a category A or B weapon to 10 years. A licence for any other category is limited to 5 years."),
    ("The longest term a Queensland licence for weapons other than category A or B can be issued for is:",
     "5 years", ["10 years", "3 years", "2 years"],
     "Under s 20(1) of the Weapons Act, a licence for a weapon other than a category A or B weapon may run for no more than 5 years, half the 10-year maximum for category A or B."),
    ("A Queensland licensee who moves house must advise the police of the new address within:",
     "14 days", ["7 days", "28 days", "3 months"],
     "Section 24 makes it a condition of every licence that the licensee advises an officer in charge of police within 14 days of a change of address and the other listed changes."),
    ("Which change must a Queensland licensee report to police within 14 days?",
     "Losing access to secure storage", ["Buying a new box of ammunition", "Changing their mobile phone plan", "Shooting at a different range"],
     "Section 24(2)(b) lists a change in the licensee's access to secure storage facilities among the changes that must be advised within 14 days, with changes of address, name and reason."),
    ("A landowner revokes the written permission a licensee relied on to shoot on rural land. The licensee must:",
     "Advise police within 14 days", ["Wait until the licence renewal", "Ask the dealer to note it", "Tell the safety instructor"],
     "Section 24(2)(f) lists the revocation of a licensee's permission to shoot on a landowner's rural land as a change that must be advised to police within 14 days."),
    ("A Queensland licensee is charged with a serious offence. Under the Act, they must:",
     "Advise police within 14 days", ["Advise police at renewal", "Advise their club only", "Advise nobody until convicted"],
     "Section 24(2)(a)(iii) includes being charged with, or convicted of, a serious offence among the changes in circumstances a licensee must advise police of within 14 days."),
    ("Unless there are exceptional circumstances, an application for a first Queensland licence cannot be decided until the end of the:",
     "28th day after lodging", ["7th day after lodging", "14th day after lodging", "90th day after lodging"],
     "Section 10 of the Weapons Regulation 2016, made for s 15 of the Act, sets the waiting period as the end of the 28th day after the application was lodged, unless an authorised officer is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances."),
    ("Under the Weapons Act 1990 (Qld), who may issue, renew or endorse a licence?",
     "An authorised officer", ["A shooting club secretary", "A licensed firearms dealer", "A safety course instructor"],
     "Section 9 of the Weapons Act says a licence may be issued, renewed, endorsed or altered only by an authorised officer. Clubs and dealers have other duties but cannot issue licences."),
    ("In deciding whether a person is fit and proper to hold a licence, an authorised officer must consider the person's:",
     "Mental and physical fitness", ["Results in club competitions", "Annual household income", "Choice of firearm brand"],
     "Section 10B of the Weapons Act requires the officer to consider, among other things, the person's mental and physical fitness, relevant offences and charges, and any domestic violence order."),
    ("Besides a genuine reason, a Queensland licence applicant must have access to:",
     "Secure storage facilities", ["A rural property to shoot on", "A licensed dealer nearby", "A licensed shooting partner"],
     "Section 10(2)(c) of the Weapons Act requires the applicant to have access to secure storage facilities for the weapons the licence will cover."),
    ("Without reasonable excuse, shortening the barrel of a firearm in Queensland is:",
     "An offence under the Act", ["Lawful for any licensee", "Lawful if a gunsmith does it", "Lawful on rural land"],
     "Section 61 of the Weapons Act makes it an offence, without reasonable excuse, to shorten a firearm, to possess a shortened firearm or to acquire or sell one."),
    ("The Weapons Act achieves its object for firearms partly by prohibiting, except in special circumstances:",
     "Self-loading rifles", ["Single shot rifles", "Break action shotguns", "Bolt action air rifles"],
     "Section 4 of the Weapons Act prohibits the possession and use of all automatic and self-loading rifles and shotguns except in special circumstances. Single shot rifles, break action shotguns and air rifles are lower categories."),
    ("The Weapons Act 1990 (Qld) sets up an integrated scheme for:",
     "Licensing and registration", ["Taxing all firearm sales", "Insuring firearm owners", "Training range officers"],
     "Section 4(b) of the Weapons Act states the object is achieved partly by establishing an integrated licensing and registration scheme for all firearms."),
    ("Under the Weapons Act, a person who wants a firearm under a licence must demonstrate:",
     "A genuine reason", ["Prior shooting experience", "A clean driving record", "Membership of two clubs"],
     "Section 4(c) requires each person who wishes to possess a firearm under a licence to demonstrate a genuine reason for possessing it, from the reasons listed in s 11 and the regulation."),
    ("Which reason does the Weapons Regulation 2016 add to the genuine reasons in the Act?",
     "A historical re-enactment", ["Guarding a home business", "Carrying cash for work", "Scaring off wildlife at home"],
     "Section 7 of the Weapons Regulation 2016 adds military or medieval re-enactments and historical demonstrations, starting sporting events, theatrical productions and paint-pellet sports. Protecting property is not a reason."),
    ("A person who keeps historic firearms for their history and value would most likely rely on which genuine reason?",
     "Collection or study", ["Recreational shooting", "Occupational requirement", "Sports or target shooting"],
     "Section 11(d) of the Weapons Act lists the collection, preservation or study of weapons as a genuine reason. Collector's licences exist for this purpose."),
    ("A grazier who needs a rifle to destroy injured stock on the property would most likely rely on:",
     "An occupational requirement", ["Recreational shooting", "Sports or target shooting", "Collection, preservation or study"],
     "Section 11(c) of the Weapons Act lists an occupational requirement, including one for rural purposes. The applicant must say why the business needs the weapon."),
    ("If an authorised officer rejects a licence application, the applicant must be given:",
     "A notice of the reasons", ["No reason of any kind", "A fresh safety course booking", "A permit to acquire instead"],
     "Section 19 of the Weapons Act requires a notice of rejection in the approved form stating the specific reasons. Where the reason is criminal intelligence, the notice may say 'confidential information'."),
    ("Which Queensland licence class covers handguns (category H) for sports or target shooting?",
     "Concealable firearms licence", ["Firearms licence", "Collector's licence (heirloom)", "Blank-fire firearms licence"],
     "Section 12 of the Weapons Act lists the concealable firearms licence as its own class, and the Weapons Regulation 2016 says what it authorises. An ordinary firearms licence covers category A and B weapons."),
]
